---
// Account deletion instructions.
//
// Google Play's User Data policy requires a publicly reachable URL, no login,
// that says how to delete an account and what deletion removes. It is submitted
// in the Data safety form, so DELETE_ACCOUNT_URL is frozen once the listing
// declares it — change the page, never the path.
//
// ONE SCREEN, deliberately. This is a utility page for someone who has already
// decided, not a landing page: it uses `.wrap .page` like /privacy and /terms,
// the steps come first, and the alternatives sit in a sidebar where they can be
// ignored. A retention wall in front of a legally-required deletion route is
// both a dark pattern and a policy violation.
//
// Every bold label below is the live English ARB string — "Delete everything",
// "Yes, delete it all", "What Ember remembers", "Sign out". If a label changes
// in lib/l10n/app_en.arb it changes here; instructions naming a button the app
// does not have are worse than none.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL, PRIVACY_URL } from '../consts';

const support = `mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your Cirrus account and everything in it — five taps inside the app, no form to send and nothing to wait for. What's removed, what stays, and what to do first if you're subscribed."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Delete account' }]}
>
  <div class="wrap page da">
    <header class="da__head">
      <h1>Delete your {SITE_TITLE} account</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        It's your data, so there are no hoops here. Five taps in the app, nothing to send us and
        nothing to wait for.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="da__cols">
      <div class="da__main">
        {/* The emoji is part of the app's own button label, so it stays — but it
            sits in its own element. Space Grotesk's word space is narrow enough
            that "⚙️ Settings" as one string reads as "⚙️Settings" on screen. */}
        <ol class="path">
          <li><b>Home</b><span>The tab the app opens on.</span></li>
          <li><b>Your avatar</b><span>The emoji circle at the top, next to your streak flame.</span></li>
          <li><b><i class="path__e">⚙️</i>Settings</b><span>The wide button at the bottom of your profile.</span></li>
          <li><b>Delete everything</b><span>In the <i class="path__e">🔒</i>Privacy card, part way down Settings.</span></li>
          <li><b>Yes, delete it all</b><span>The one confirmation. There's no undo after it.</span></li>
        </ol>

        {/* True of the live backend — functions/src/handlers/deleteUserData.ts
            anonymises posts and explicitly leaves the store subscription alone.
            The subscription line is the only thing on this page that costs a
            person money if we stay quiet about it, so it leads. */}
        <p class="da__note">
          <b>Cancel your subscription first.</b> Google Play and Apple do the billing, not us, so
          deleting the account doesn't stop it — and the in-app shortcut goes with the account.{' '}
          <b>Settings → Manage subscription</b> opens the right page while you still have it.
        </p>

        <h2>What goes</h2>
        <p>
          Your plan and curve, every puff, craving and mood you logged, your streak, badges and
          goals, your whole conversation with Ember and everything it remembered, and the login
          itself. No queue, no review, no way back — signing up again starts a real day one.
        </p>

        <h2>What stays</h2>
        <p>
          Posts and replies you left in the community, so threads other people are in don't
          develop holes. The words stay, your name doesn't: they're relabelled{' '}
          <b>[departed quitter]</b> and the private link between you and them is destroyed.
          Detail in the <a href={PRIVACY_URL}>privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Can't get in?</h2>
        <p>
          Your account is on our servers, not the phone, so uninstalling didn't delete it —
          reinstall, sign in, and the steps work as written. Can't sign in at all? Write from the
          email address on the account. A guest account has no email to match, so that one can
          only be deleted from a phone still signed in.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="da__aside" aria-labelledby="smaller">
        <h2 id="smaller">Smaller than deleting</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Settings → Notifications</b> turns every push off. Or move the one that matters with <b>Danger hours</b>.</li>
          <li>Cancel the subscription and keep the account. The free tier isn't a trial — it doesn't run out.</li>
          <li><b>Settings → What Ember remembers</b> lists everything the coach kept, and deletes any of it.</li>
          <li><b>Settings → Sign out</b> leaves it all on your account. The streak keeps burning.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="da__ask">
          Whichever way you go, tell us what pushed you here — one line is plenty, and it's read
          by the person who built the app.<br />
          <a href={support}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Tighter than `.page`'s default: this is a one-scroll utility page and the
     breadcrumb already sits above it. */
  .da { padding-block: clamp(4px, 1vw, 12px) clamp(44px, 6vw, 64px); }
  .da__head { max-width: 42rem; }
  .da h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.2vw, 2.6rem); }
  .da .lede { margin: 0.9rem 0 0; max-width: 46ch; font-size: 1.0625rem; }

  .da__cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .da__main { min-width: 0; }
  .da__main h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .da__main p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    /* The path card fills the column; the prose under it keeps a measure. */
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  /* Bold is an in-app label everywhere on this page — the reader learns once
     that anything bold is something they will literally see on their phone. */
  .da b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .da a { text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }

  /* ---------- the path ---------- */

  /* A counter, not list markers: the numeral sits in a 26px disc that has to
     share a baseline with the label beside it, which list-style cannot do. */
  .path {
    counter-reset: step;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--lift);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .path li {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr;
    /* Row gap 0: the label and its hint are one block, and a shared row gap
       here pushed every step to 100px tall. */
    gap: 0 13px;
    padding: 11px clamp(15px, 2.5vw, 20px);
  }
  .path li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

  .path li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    grid-row: span 2;
    align-self: start;
    margin-top: 1px;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--slate);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--volt);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* The last step is the irreversible one, and it wears the app's own
     destructive colour. The only tinted marker on the page. */
  .path li:last-child::before {
    background: rgb(255 92 92 / 0.14);
    border-color: rgb(255 92 92 / 0.5);
    color: var(--relapse);
  }

  .path b {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .path span {
    grid-column: 2;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .path__e { font-style: normal; margin-right: 0.4em; }

  /* ---------- the money warning ---------- */

  .da__note {
    margin: 18px 0 0 !important;
    max-width: none !important;
    padding: 13px 15px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ember);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--lift);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  /* ---------- sidebar ---------- */

  .da__aside h2 {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .da__aside ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .da__aside li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 12px 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .da__ask {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (min-width: 58rem) {
    .da__cols { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16.5rem; }
    /* Sticky so the alternatives stay offerable while the reader is in the
       detail below, without costing them a second screen of their own. */
    .da__aside { position: sticky; top: 24px; }
  }
</style>
